/**
  @page guides-meshes-io Mesh input/output
  @brief Saving and loading meshes

  @tableofcontents

  @m_footernavigation

  Rodin supports reading and writing meshes in various file formats through
  the @ref Rodin::IO "IO" module.

  @section guides-meshes-io-intro Introduction

  Mesh I/O operations provide:
  - Load meshes from external mesh generators
  - Save computed meshes for later use
  - Exchange meshes with other software
  - Archive simulation data

  @section guides-meshes-io-formats Supported formats

  The file format is specified explicitly via the
  @ref Rodin::IO::FileFormat "IO::FileFormat" enumeration:

  | Format | Extension | Description |
  |--------|-----------|-------------|
  | MFEM | `.mesh` | MFEM native format |
  | MEDIT | `.mesh` | MEDIT format from INRIA (used by MMG) |
  | HDF5 | `.h5` | High-performance binary format |

  @section guides-meshes-io-loading Loading meshes

  @subsection guides-meshes-io-loading-basic Basic loading

  Use @ref Rodin::Geometry::Mesh "Mesh::load()" with an explicit
  @ref Rodin::IO::FileFormat "IO::FileFormat":

  @code{.cpp}
  #include <Rodin/Geometry.h>

  using namespace Rodin;
  using namespace Rodin::Geometry;

  int main()
  {
    Mesh mesh;

    // Load MFEM format
    mesh.load("domain.mfem.mesh", IO::FileFormat::MFEM);

    // Load MEDIT format
    mesh.load("domain.medit.mesh", IO::FileFormat::MEDIT);

    return 0;
  }
  @endcode

  @section guides-meshes-io-saving Saving meshes

  @subsection guides-meshes-io-saving-basic Basic saving

  Use @ref Rodin::Geometry::Mesh "Mesh::save()" with an explicit format:

  @code{.cpp}
  Mesh mesh;
  mesh = mesh.UniformGrid(Polytope::Type::Triangle, {16, 16});

  // Save in MFEM format
  mesh.save("output.mfem.mesh", IO::FileFormat::MFEM);

  // Save in MEDIT format
  mesh.save("output.medit.mesh", IO::FileFormat::MEDIT);
  @endcode

  @subsection guides-meshes-io-saving-medit MEDIT format

  The MEDIT format is commonly used with the
  @ref Rodin::MMG "MMG" mesh adaptation tools:

  @code{.cpp}
  mesh.save("domain.mesh", IO::FileFormat::MEDIT);
  @endcode

  @section guides-meshes-io-example Complete example

  @snippet IO/MEDIT.cpp medit-source

  The generated input makes the program self-contained. Its output files use
  distinct names for each representation.

  @section guides-meshes-io-external External mesh generators

  @subsection guides-meshes-io-external-mmg MMG

  [MMG](https://www.mmgtools.org/) is used for mesh adaptation and
  optimization. Rodin integrates directly with MMG through the
  @ref Rodin::MMG "MMG" module. See the
  @ref examples-mmg-index "MMG examples" for details.

  @section guides-meshes-io-paths File paths

  @subsection guides-meshes-io-paths-absolute Absolute paths

  @code{.cpp}
  mesh.load("/home/user/meshes/domain.mesh", IO::FileFormat::MFEM);
  @endcode

  @subsection guides-meshes-io-paths-relative Relative paths

  Relative paths are resolved from the executable's working directory. Create
  output directories before saving files into them.

  @code{.cpp}
  mesh.load("../data/domain.mesh", IO::FileFormat::MFEM);
  mesh.save("./output/result.mesh", IO::FileFormat::MFEM);
  @endcode

  @section guides-meshes-io-considerations Format considerations

  @subsection guides-meshes-io-considerations-compatibility Compatibility

  - **MFEM**: Best for MFEM-based workflows
  - **MEDIT**: Required for MMG tools

  @subsection guides-meshes-io-considerations-attributes Attributes

  Select a supported mesh representation and verify its round trip. The core
  geometry data comprises:
  - Vertex coordinates
  - Element connectivity
  - Element attributes (region markers)
  - Boundary attributes

  @section guides-meshes-io-see-also See also

  - @ref guides-io "I/O in Rodin" — Comprehensive I/O guide including XDMF
  - @ref guides-meshes-creation "Mesh creation"
  - @ref guides-meshes "Meshes overview"
  - @ref Rodin::IO "I/O namespace"

  */
